A simple boolean flag wrapping a new code path. The flag service decides per-request whether to take the new path.

```java
@RestController
public class CheckoutController {
  private final FeatureFlagClient flags;
  private final NewCheckoutService newSvc;
  private final OldCheckoutService oldSvc;

  @PostMapping("/checkout")
  public CheckoutResponse checkout(@RequestBody CheckoutRequest req,
                                   Principal user) {
    if (flags.isEnabled("new-checkout-flow", user.getName())) {
      return newSvc.process(req);
    }
    return oldSvc.process(req);
  }
}
```

The flag client (LaunchDarkly, Unleash, etc.) caches flag values locally and polls the flag service every 30 seconds. The latency cost per request is microseconds. The targeting logic lives in the flag service — percentage rollout, user lists, geo targeting, or custom rules — without code changes.

**Targeting examples** the flag service typically supports:
- 5% of all users (consistent per user via hash)
- All users in segment `internal-employees`
- All users with country = `US`
- Specific user IDs (for QA testing in prod)
- A/B test cohorts with stable assignment
